{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And they pursued.</b> It is the usage of the language to say thus, as in \"and all the people saw…\" and \"the people saw and trembled\" (below 20:15), the meaning being: when they saw, they trembled and stood afar off. And so it is written \"and he pursued after the children of Israel\" (above, parashah 5 [Exodus 14:8]). Now the meaning of וירדפו is: when they pursued after them, they overtook them encamping by the sea." "And he mentioned \"all Pharaoh's horses\" because they did not come scattered, but all together." "And his horsemen are the riders of the horses." "And his host — foot soldiers."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:22.978576438Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}